<title>RUSSIA: Russian Duma approves 1997 government borrowing.</title>
<headline>Russian Duma approves 1997 government borrowing.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian State Duma lower house of parliament voted 308 to three with no abstentions on Monday to approve a programme of government borrowing for 1997.</p>
<p>The Duma takes the final decision on such matters.</p>
<p>The overall volume of external state borrowing in 1997 will total $9.8 billion, of which $7.3 billion are credits without conditions and $2.5 billion are conditional.</p>
<p>Credits without conditions are as follows:</p>
<p>(million dollars)</p>
<p> International Monetary Fund		    2,800</p>
<p> World Bank					   1,100</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>    loan for social structural reform	    250</p>
<p>    loan for reform of budget process	    600</p>
<p>    loan for coal sector restructuring	   250</p>
<p> External bonds					3,400</p>
<p>Conditional credits are as follows:</p>
<p> World Bank					     576</p>
<p>European Bank for</p>
<p>    Reconstruction and Development		 24</p>
<p> Foreign governments				1,503</p>
<p> Foreign commercial banks and firms	     397</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
